The CSIPHY reset sequence, like the vendor's

It is the last divergence left with Qualcomm's driver across the whole CSIPHY
path. Their reset table for version 1.2 (csiphy_reset_reg_1_2) first turns off
the three common-block registers and WAITS, and only then pulses the reset:

    {0x0814, 0x00, wait 5 ms}   <- remove the lane enable
    {0x0818, 0x00}
    {0x081C, 0x00}
    {0x0800, 0x01, wait 1 ms}   <- reset pulse
    {0x0800, 0x00}

Mainline only pulses 0x0800 and leaves the other three as they were.

The rest of the path is already cross-checked and matches: the lane table is an
EXACT copy of csiphy_2ph_v1_2_reg -115 out of 115 entries, same order, same
values, checked automatically-, the common block is corrected to version 1.2
(0060) and the clocks completed (0063).
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c	2026-08-17 00:56:17.489351351 +0200
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c	2026-08-17 00:56:45.461680256 +0200
@@ -957,6 +957,29 @@
 
 	printk(KERN_DEBUG "csiphy_reset id %d with base %p and offset %d\n", csiphy->id, csiphy->base, regs->offset);
 
+	/*
+	 * The Qualcomm driver (csiphy_reset_reg_1_2) first clears the three
+	 * common block registers and WAITS, and only then pulses the reset:
+	 *
+	 *     {0x0814, 0x00, wait 5 ms}   <- clear the lane enable
+	 *     {0x0818, 0x00}
+	 *     {0x081C, 0x00}
+	 *     {0x0800, 0x01, wait 1 ms}     <- the reset pulse
+	 *     {0x0800, 0x00}
+	 *
+	 * Mainline only pulses 0x0800 and leaves the other three as they were. It is
+	 * the last divergence left from the vendor flow: the lane
+	 * table is an exact copy (115 of 115 entries), the common block is
+	 * already fixed up to version 1.2 and so are the clocks.
+	 */
+	writel_relaxed(0x0, csiphy->base +
+		       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 5));
+	usleep_range(5000, 6000);
+	writel_relaxed(0x0, csiphy->base +
+		       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 6));
+	writel_relaxed(0x0, csiphy->base +
+		       CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 7));
+
 	writel_relaxed(0x1, csiphy->base +
 		      CSIPHY_3PH_CMN_CSI_COMMON_CTRLn(regs->offset, 0));
 	usleep_range(5000, 8000);
